    "summary": "High‑energy ’69 set with soaring Dark Star > St Stephen > Eleven",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering first half that builds into a massive Dark Star → Saint Stephen → The Eleven suite, followed by an extended Other One → Alligator → Caution trek. Morning Dew and the wild Feedback jam round out a night of adventurous playing despite a fuzzy tape.",
    "review": "What unfolds at The Music Box on February 4, 1969 finds the Dead in peak early‑rock form. Jerry’s guitar is on fire, carving dynamic phrases through Dark Star that lift into crystalline leads on Saint Stephen and cascade into the frantic pulse of The Eleven. The second half escalates with a monster Other One → Alligator → Caution sequence where the band locks into an exploratory groove, punctuated by a raw, feedback‑laden jam to close the set. While the soundboard source is marred by tape hiss, speed anomalies and occasional drum drop‑outs, the mix remains balanced enough to hear every instrument, and the organ sits deep but audible, adding texture to the improvisations. For anyone chasing early Dead intensity, this recording captures a night of high‑octane playing that stands out in the 1969 catalog.",
